WEBVTT

00:01.890 --> 00:04.290
<i>Has everyone made their</i> <i>plans for Golden Week?</i>

00:04.500 --> 00:07.960
<i>And so, once again, it's time</i> <i>to say goodbye for the day.</i>

00:08.200 --> 00:10.860
<i>This is Asahi Sakurai, signing off.</i>

00:11.140 --> 00:12.870
<i>Now, here's our last song.</i>

00:13.070 --> 00:15.100
<i>It's a new song from Childish An Hour...</i>

00:20.110 --> 00:21.740
I guess I fell asleep.

00:29.820 --> 00:31.480
It's already the day after tomorrow.

00:31.560 --> 00:33.890
It's the deadline,

00:31.560 --> 00:33.890
my brother!

00:40.470 --> 00:43.160
What?! An exhibition and spot sale?!

00:47.370 --> 00:49.860
What do you mean by an exhibition and spot sale?

00:51.280 --> 00:52.540
Not to worry.

00:52.610 --> 00:54.940
I have already completed the application.

00:55.210 --> 00:56.210
GROUPS, APPLY NOW! (DEADLINE MARCH 20)
SPONSORED BY COMIC BRAVO COMMITTEE

00:55.210 --> 00:58.580
COMIC BRAVO

00:55.210 --> 00:58.580
MAY 6 (MON)

00:55.210 --> 00:58.580
IKEBUKURO SHINE PARK CITY

00:59.990 --> 01:01.750
And then there was light!

01:01.920 --> 01:03.650
Yes, just as in God's Book of Genesis,

01:03.760 --> 01:06.020
this day will eventually be carved into history.

01:06.360 --> 01:09.090
It shall become the first day to achieving our ambition.

01:11.800 --> 01:12.760
What is it?

01:12.830 --> 01:14.270
This deadline.

01:14.330 --> 01:17.330
It's even earlier than the day we went to Odaiba.

01:15.330 --> 01:17.330
(DEADLINE MARCH 20)

01:19.340 --> 01:21.540
You were planning on setting me up from the start, weren't you?

01:21.540 --> 01:23.700
It was a divine message, Comrade Kazuki.

01:24.540 --> 01:26.380
Having been told by the three wise kings of Bethlehem...

01:26.380 --> 01:29.780
...that your eyes would unfailingly open to the world of doujinshi,

01:29.910 --> 01:32.650
I took this calculated course of action!

01:33.690 --> 01:34.850
What is that?

01:35.020 --> 01:36.720
Aren't they students from our school?

01:36.790 --> 01:38.480
They seem really sketchy.

01:40.860 --> 01:42.830
I get it. I get it, okay?

01:44.760 --> 01:48.290
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

01:48.830 --> 01:51.970
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

01:51.970 --> 01:55.530
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

01:55.770 --> 01:58.800
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

01:59.080 --> 02:02.710
<i>It just doesn't get across...</i>
<i>Nani o Shite mo Tsutawarazu</i>

02:02.710 --> 02:06.280
<i>It's just not working right at all.</i>
<i>Umaku Ikanai Bakari de</i>

02:06.280 --> 02:09.620
<i>But even I and everyone else...</i>
<i>Watashi Datte Dare Datte</i>

02:09.850 --> 02:13.350
<i>... have times like that.</i>
<i>Atarimae ni Aru Koto</i>

02:13.460 --> 02:16.830
<i>Those things that don't return to your heart.</i>
<i>Mune no Naka ni Kaeranai</i>

02:17.030 --> 02:20.430
<i>But even those words and feelings...</i>
<i>Omoi mo Kotoba mo Itsuka</i>

02:20.600 --> 02:25.000
<i>... will come back in time someday...</i>
<i>Jikan ga Tateba Modotte Kuru kara</i>

02:25.240 --> 02:28.140
<i>... before you know it.</i>
<i>Shiranai Uchi ni</i>

02:28.440 --> 02:34.350
<i>There's only one thing you can do right now.</i>
<i>Ima Kimiga Dekiru Koto wa Hitotsu</i>

02:34.710 --> 02:41.410
<i>Just accept it and go with it.</i>
<i>Sono Mama Ukeirete Yukou</i>

02:42.090 --> 02:46.090
<i>Just be you and stay true to yourself.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Itsuwarazu ni</i>

02:46.090 --> 02:49.260
<i>Take a little break.</i>
<i>Sukoshi Hitoyasumi Shite</i>

02:49.260 --> 02:53.000
<i>Take your impatience and your hardships...</i>
<i>Aseru Kimochi Kurushii Koto</i>

02:53.000 --> 02:56.260
<i>...and turn them into your strengths.</i>
<i>Kimi no Power ni Kaete</i>

02:56.370 --> 03:00.130
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

03:00.470 --> 03:03.580
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

03:03.580 --> 03:07.170
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

03:07.380 --> 03:10.310
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

03:13.350 --> 03:20.160
INTO IT

03:13.350 --> 03:20.160
PUT YOUR HEART

03:22.230 --> 03:25.820
But I've never properly drawn a comic before.

03:26.230 --> 03:27.790
Nothin' to worry about.

03:27.870 --> 03:30.840
It's a doujinshi, just draw whatever you want.

03:34.810 --> 03:35.800
When in the world?!

03:36.670 --> 03:39.010
Better to have as many people with experience as possible, right?

03:39.710 --> 03:40.910
Very well!

03:41.550 --> 03:43.740
You have my permission to join us, Comrade.

03:44.720 --> 03:45.910
What?!

03:46.650 --> 03:48.780
I don't have any doujin friends over here,

03:48.890 --> 03:51.650
so I figured this'd be the perfect way to kill time.

03:52.090 --> 03:53.720
But what about that other girl?

03:54.260 --> 03:57.490
Remember? The one from the group called Cat or something?

03:57.860 --> 04:00.400
Oh, you mean Eimi.
She's no friend of mine.

04:00.400 --> 04:01.470
But...

04:00.770 --> 04:02.270
This is terrible!

04:02.270 --> 04:05.760
This place's original burger really tastes super-terrible!

04:07.340 --> 04:08.700
H-hey, that's my...

04:08.810 --> 04:10.240
Why the heck are you here?!

04:10.540 --> 04:13.670
I heard that the panda came down from the mountains of Kobe...

04:13.750 --> 04:17.270
...to the great city of Tokyo, so I came to see for myself.

04:18.020 --> 04:18.980
Go home! Go home!

04:18.980 --> 04:22.150
Country pandas should just go home to the mountains of Kobe!

04:22.490 --> 04:23.820
Well, what do you say we get going?

04:24.060 --> 04:25.460
Yes, I agree.

04:25.720 --> 04:29.130
Hey, how dare you ignore me, you're just a country panda!

04:29.190 --> 04:30.590
That super-pisses me off!

04:30.660 --> 04:33.390
Wanna drop by a convenience store and buy some stuff?

04:33.460 --> 04:34.630
W-wait...

04:34.700 --> 04:36.690
Hurry up or the sun's gonna set!

04:42.170 --> 04:43.640
I see, I see how it is.

04:43.740 --> 04:46.300
You're running because you're terrified of my talent.

04:47.380 --> 04:48.710
That's it, isn't it?!

04:48.280 --> 04:50.410
Oh, look! It's a cylindrical UFO!

04:50.520 --> 04:51.480
What?!

04:51.620 --> 04:52.950
Where?! Where?!

04:53.690 --> 04:55.480
I don't see it!

04:55.990 --> 04:58.290
There's nothing there! Where is it?!

04:59.690 --> 05:01.960
Did you hear that? A UFO.

05:00.990 --> 05:01.960
That is so odd.

05:02.130 --> 05:03.560
Maybe she's a little kooky.

05:06.330 --> 05:08.270
That super-pisses me off!

05:13.710 --> 05:15.700
So, where are we really going, anyway?

05:16.510 --> 05:17.910
First, we must hammer into you...

05:17.910 --> 05:19.940
...everything there is to know about doujinshi.

05:20.140 --> 05:22.200
And to do that, we will head to our hideout.

05:22.650 --> 05:23.880
Hideout?

05:23.980 --> 05:27.510
Yes! In other words, a gathering place of ambitious men!

05:27.650 --> 05:29.380
Or you could even call it Tokiwasou!

05:29.850 --> 05:31.690
Th-that would be...

05:31.690 --> 05:32.880
That would be?

05:33.260 --> 05:34.120
That would be...

05:40.870 --> 05:42.270
It's my place.

05:43.170 --> 05:44.760
URU-URU

05:43.170 --> 05:44.760
MART

05:45.040 --> 05:45.970
"Manjien"

05:46.270 --> 05:47.830
Well, shall we begin?

05:47.970 --> 05:48.670
Sure.

05:48.670 --> 05:52.970
First, we'll start with choosing a genre for the doujinshi you'll create.

05:53.180 --> 05:54.370
"Jungle"?

05:54.710 --> 05:56.980
Wrong! Too bad! 5 points off!

05:57.520 --> 05:59.110
Behold this!

06:00.220 --> 06:02.280
And this and this and this!

06:02.590 --> 06:03.950
And this one, too!

06:09.030 --> 06:11.290
This is the character you drew the other day...

06:11.930 --> 06:14.760
Parody!!!

06:14.970 --> 06:19.800
[ Parody ]

06:14.970 --> 06:19.800
Something that takes the essence

06:14.970 --> 06:19.800
of a preexisting or famous work

06:14.970 --> 06:19.800
and comically imitates its style

06:14.970 --> 06:19.800
and characteristics.

06:14.970 --> 06:19.800
Spoof. Cheap fiction.

06:14.970 --> 06:19.800
Works parodying anime in

06:14.970 --> 06:19.800
particular are abbreviated

06:14.970 --> 06:19.800
as "ani-paro".

06:20.970 --> 06:22.140
That is all.

06:22.140 --> 06:25.130
Does that mean the ones you write are parodies, too, Miss Inagawa?

06:25.380 --> 06:26.440
Freakin' moron!

06:26.440 --> 06:30.710
My books may be parodies, but they're a different kind of parody!

06:30.850 --> 06:34.150
They're an homage to the original, drawn passionately from the soul!

06:34.420 --> 06:35.550
Homage?

06:35.620 --> 06:36.610
Yes!

06:36.890 --> 06:41.720
[ Homage ]

06:36.890 --> 06:41.720
A word originally meaning

06:36.890 --> 06:41.720
"respect" or "to pledge (loyalty)".

06:36.890 --> 06:41.720
It has come to refer to creating

06:36.890 --> 06:41.720
new works based on a deep

06:36.890 --> 06:41.720
admiration for a specific work

06:36.890 --> 06:41.720
with content similar to the

06:36.890 --> 06:41.720
original.

06:42.930 --> 06:44.450
That pretty much covers it.

06:44.700 --> 06:45.820
I see.

06:46.200 --> 06:48.360
Never mind that.
Quit callin' me "Miss Inagawa"!

06:48.430 --> 06:49.770
It gives me the creeps!

06:49.770 --> 06:50.740
What? But...

06:50.740 --> 06:51.770
Just call me "Yuu".

06:51.770 --> 06:52.960
O-okay.

06:53.340 --> 06:56.270
And the other one is original!

06:56.510 --> 07:01.280
(As opposed to a reproduction)
An original work. Refers to unique works based on the artist's own ideas and not dependent on references to other works.
Furthermore, an original character is sometimes called an "ori-char" for short.

06:56.510 --> 07:01.280
[ Original ]

07:03.210 --> 07:06.550
Then, since I don't know many recent anime shows,

07:06.620 --> 07:07.710
I guess I'll go with original.

07:07.890 --> 07:09.180
What?!

07:09.790 --> 07:11.220
For real?!

07:11.990 --> 07:14.720
Original is a field where the author's skill and individuality...

07:14.790 --> 07:16.690
...are in the open for all to see!

07:16.990 --> 07:19.130
Right! They also tend to be too sober...

07:19.130 --> 07:22.930
...and they're tough to sell with a new, no-name writer.

07:23.000 --> 07:24.000
Look!

07:24.000 --> 07:25.440
What is wrong with this?!

07:26.070 --> 07:27.330
Surely, it is familiar to you!

07:27.410 --> 07:30.340
You should be able to create a parody of this work!

07:30.880 --> 07:32.640
You say it so suddenly...

07:32.780 --> 07:34.610
Oh, Hiroyuki.

07:34.680 --> 07:37.050
What the heck? You know "To Heart"?

07:37.450 --> 07:38.950
Oh, no, it was in my dream once.

07:38.950 --> 07:39.920
Dream?

07:39.980 --> 07:41.610
Why the heck would ya dream about an anime you don't know?

07:45.420 --> 07:46.520
Behold!

07:46.860 --> 07:48.660
<i>I'm falling! I'm falling!</i>

07:50.930 --> 07:53.560
<i>I can't hold on anymore!</i>

07:51.500 --> 07:55.160
This is the mysterious sleep-learning device that I planted...

07:55.270 --> 07:57.830
...in order to give you the basis for a parody.

07:58.140 --> 08:02.510
I call it the power of "Mr.
Revelation from the Heavens #2"!

08:02.670 --> 08:03.870
Um...

08:07.880 --> 08:09.070
Sheesh!

08:09.410 --> 08:12.040
What's with him having something suddenly come up?!

08:16.150 --> 08:19.280
He promised to go to today's concert a long time ago.

08:24.300 --> 08:25.460
Something sudden...

08:25.900 --> 08:27.260
I-it can't be!

08:29.030 --> 08:32.830
I understand well your desire to try your hand with an original work.

08:33.870 --> 08:35.770
You're surprisingly understanding about this...

08:35.870 --> 08:37.070
However!

08:37.880 --> 08:39.710
Original? Fine!

08:39.710 --> 08:41.940
But in order to secure a certain number of sales,

08:42.010 --> 08:44.480
catchy and exciting art is absolutely necessary!

08:44.580 --> 08:46.140
Do you understand?! Exciting!

08:46.450 --> 08:47.350
Exciting?

08:48.220 --> 08:49.190
L-like this?!

08:50.620 --> 08:52.280
And yaaa!

08:52.920 --> 08:54.290
Wrong "exciting"!

08:54.460 --> 08:57.290
No real

08:54.460 --> 08:57.290
explanation

08:54.460 --> 08:57.290
necessary.

08:54.460 --> 08:57.290
Example -

08:54.460 --> 08:57.290
<i>Cute Yuu with</i>

08:54.460 --> 08:57.290
[ Moe ]

08:54.460 --> 08:57.290
<i>the glasses is</i>

08:54.460 --> 08:57.290
"Burning"

08:54.460 --> 08:57.290
INCORRECT

08:54.460 --> 08:57.290
<i>exciting.</i>

08:54.460 --> 08:57.290
[ Moe ]

08:54.460 --> 08:57.290
"To Sprout"

08:54.460 --> 08:57.290
CORRECT

08:57.860 --> 08:59.420
For instance, things like this!

09:08.810 --> 09:11.570
You draw in the audience with catchy art such as this,

09:11.640 --> 09:13.840
but you create the work true to yourself!

09:14.010 --> 09:17.610
This is strategic calculation!
A mature concept, if you will!

09:18.850 --> 09:21.450
<i>Oh, Hiroyuki!</i>

09:24.660 --> 09:26.750
Now, say it with me!

09:26.990 --> 09:28.150
What?

09:33.500 --> 09:34.690
I knew it!

09:37.240 --> 09:38.500
What?!

09:42.210 --> 09:43.140
Mi-Mizuki...

09:44.210 --> 09:45.140
What in the...

09:45.340 --> 09:48.140
N-no, this isn't what it...

09:48.210 --> 09:50.650
You skipped out on your promise about the concert...

09:50.980 --> 09:53.880
N-no, it's research for doujinshi...

09:56.620 --> 09:59.990
Wha... What the heck are you doing?!

10:04.860 --> 10:06.300
She's right...

10:10.300 --> 10:13.030
What the heck am I doing?

10:33.390 --> 10:35.380
Owowow...

10:41.770 --> 10:44.400
I wonder if Mizuki's still mad...

10:49.610 --> 10:52.510
Rise! Bow!

11:02.350 --> 11:03.790
What're you going to do about lunch?

11:03.850 --> 11:04.920
What?

11:04.920 --> 11:06.020
Oh...

11:06.260 --> 11:08.320
You've been drawing all this time, right?

11:08.390 --> 11:09.550
Yeah, sort of.

11:09.660 --> 11:12.990
I've liked your drawings ever since middle school, but...

11:13.660 --> 11:14.790
But?

11:17.100 --> 11:20.370
So, are you serious about this doujinshi thing?

11:20.740 --> 11:21.710
What?

11:21.710 --> 11:25.770
Yeah, it seems like fun, so
I thought I'd try it just once.

11:26.080 --> 11:29.570
Fun?! Where's the fun in being crammed in those hot and smelly places...

11:29.650 --> 11:32.080
...buying and selling otaku-ish books?

11:32.450 --> 11:35.050
Hey, aren't you bein' just a tad narrow-minded?!

11:35.790 --> 11:38.690
Those books might seem stupid to you,

11:38.790 --> 11:40.950
but we're all serious about writin' 'em!

11:41.190 --> 11:44.790
And there're plenty of customers who enjoy readin' 'em, too!

11:45.030 --> 11:46.550
Just 'cause you can't understand it,

11:47.000 --> 11:49.330
you don't gotta push your values onto other people!

11:50.770 --> 11:52.070
Am I wrong?

11:53.470 --> 11:54.440
Well?!

11:57.140 --> 11:59.630
Kazuki, you jerk!

12:01.050 --> 12:02.670
Why am I the one...?

12:02.950 --> 12:05.210
You just had to play right into Taishi's plan!

12:06.150 --> 12:07.580
Jerk, jerk, jerk!

12:08.790 --> 12:10.380
Hey, Mizuki!

12:17.630 --> 12:18.820
Kazuki.

12:19.200 --> 12:20.560
While you're at it,

12:20.560 --> 12:23.360
purchase a fried noodle bread and curry bread for me at the shop.

12:30.110 --> 12:32.670
Where the heck did Mizuki go?

12:36.610 --> 12:37.880
I'm falling! I'm falling!

12:49.490 --> 12:50.650
You're...

12:52.400 --> 12:54.830
Mr. Lifesaver!

12:58.100 --> 13:00.470
So you're a student here, too.

13:00.540 --> 13:04.200
But I wasn't enrolled at the time we met.

13:04.340 --> 13:05.400
I see.

13:05.980 --> 13:07.670
Here we are.

13:08.350 --> 13:09.540
There we go.

13:10.050 --> 13:11.680
Thank you very much.

13:11.680 --> 13:13.010
Later, then.

13:13.550 --> 13:16.420
Thank you very much for saving me twice.

13:17.020 --> 13:18.920
My name is Chisa Tsukamoto.

13:19.360 --> 13:22.520
I'm Kazuki Sendou.
I'm a senior. Nice to meet you.

13:22.730 --> 13:24.220
The pleasure is all mine!

13:24.500 --> 13:25.660
See you around.

13:36.910 --> 13:38.340
Say, Mizuki...

13:38.880 --> 13:40.210
Comrade Kazuki!

13:41.810 --> 13:45.010
As the second step to achieving our great ambition,

13:45.150 --> 13:48.140
we will go check out the printers!

13:49.050 --> 13:50.320
No, more importantly...

13:54.060 --> 13:55.120
What is it?

13:55.190 --> 13:56.820
No, nothing.

13:57.860 --> 14:00.160
So, what were you saying? Printing?

14:00.360 --> 14:01.260
Yes.

14:01.370 --> 14:03.430
You print doujinshi?

14:03.670 --> 14:04.970
Of course you do.

14:04.970 --> 14:08.410
You weren't plannin' on hand-drawin' dozens of copies, were you?

14:08.470 --> 14:09.610
What about photocopying?

14:09.610 --> 14:11.940
That is nonsense, my brother!

14:12.580 --> 14:15.710
Of course, there are advantages to the flexibility of photocopied issues!

14:15.850 --> 14:18.440
However, that is the equivalent of a motorboat!

14:19.580 --> 14:23.450
We, who aim to achieve our ambition, must ultimately choose...

14:24.020 --> 14:26.860
...the aircraft carrier of the doujinshi world, offset printing!

14:27.360 --> 14:28.850
So, let us go.

14:30.390 --> 14:31.450
Oh, hey!

14:32.700 --> 14:35.260
Maybe I should've invited
Mizuki along, after all.

14:35.730 --> 14:39.830
No, no, especially since that girl seems to hate doujinshi.

14:40.140 --> 14:44.100
I'll bet. She just had a terrible time at Odaiba the other day.

14:44.180 --> 14:46.870
Though, there might be other reasons for it, too.

14:48.850 --> 14:51.110
This is it, my brother!

14:51.380 --> 14:54.350
"Tsukamoto Printers"

14:58.760 --> 15:01.450
It's kind of dirty here...

15:01.690 --> 15:02.760
Absurd!

15:02.760 --> 15:06.860
Know this! Truly beautiful things are born out of this chaos!

15:07.430 --> 15:10.700
Yes! Just as life was born out of the primordial sea...

15:10.700 --> 15:12.830
...several hundred million years ago!

15:13.140 --> 15:15.000
But there isn't anybody here.

15:15.410 --> 15:18.170
Hello, there! Hello, there!

15:18.410 --> 15:19.570
Yes, Sir!

15:22.350 --> 15:23.810
Welcome!

15:24.220 --> 15:25.620
Hey, you're...

15:25.920 --> 15:29.350
Yet another coincidence, isn't it?

15:32.220 --> 15:34.190
These are the estimates.

15:37.230 --> 15:39.220
Well, these are conscientious rates.

15:40.100 --> 15:41.330
We will take this deal.

15:41.900 --> 15:44.160
All right, thank you very much.

15:44.440 --> 15:46.700
Do you help out at the shop a lot?

15:47.100 --> 15:50.410
Yes, I do. We run the shop with just us family members.

15:50.410 --> 15:51.310
Wow.

15:52.940 --> 15:54.040
What's this?

15:54.110 --> 15:56.140
That just came off the printers.

15:57.350 --> 16:01.910
I see. The blacks aren't faded and the fine tones aren't mashed.

16:02.290 --> 16:04.450
The bindin' is sturdy, too.

16:05.790 --> 16:07.120
I am happy to hear it.

16:07.320 --> 16:09.920
Is the finished quality different depending on price, after all?

16:10.160 --> 16:11.650
It is not the money!

16:12.030 --> 16:12.890
What?

16:12.960 --> 16:16.060
Mr. Ink and Mr. Paper both know very well...

16:16.330 --> 16:18.430
...the intensity of heart the artist puts into the drawings.

16:18.940 --> 16:20.060
Intensity of heart...

16:20.540 --> 16:22.010
With drawings like that,

16:22.010 --> 16:25.440
even when we use the same exact procedure and machines,

16:26.010 --> 16:28.670
the finished quality mysteriously turns out to be very beautiful.

16:29.150 --> 16:30.240
Wow...

16:30.980 --> 16:32.610
What a wonderful story.

16:32.750 --> 16:34.410
It's a bit cheesy smellin' though.

16:34.490 --> 16:35.680
Smell?

16:38.660 --> 16:40.920
I used the wrong consistency of ink!

17:01.110 --> 17:03.240
I'm really getting short on time...

17:11.320 --> 17:12.290
Hello?

17:12.290 --> 17:14.660
<i>You were... You were</i> <i>drawing again, weren't you?</i>

17:15.430 --> 17:16.420
<i>Mizuki...</i>

17:16.490 --> 17:18.220
<i>Are you telepathic or something?</i>

17:18.830 --> 17:20.760
I can tell even without special powers!

17:20.930 --> 17:22.870
You were drawing all during class, too.

17:23.470 --> 17:25.400
<i>I see. Yeah, I guess you're right.</i>

17:25.640 --> 17:27.400
I wanted to go to that concert...

17:27.770 --> 17:28.860
<i>Sorry...</i>

17:29.640 --> 17:30.870
Tomorrow!

17:30.410 --> 17:31.400
<i>What?</i>

17:31.510 --> 17:34.950
As punishment, come with me to a shop with good herbal teas, okay?!

17:35.210 --> 17:36.940
You'll be treating, naturally.

17:38.780 --> 17:40.010
You'll come, won't you?

17:40.920 --> 17:42.110
Sorry...

17:42.720 --> 17:44.710
I haven't finished the manuscript yet, so...

17:46.390 --> 17:47.520
Mizuki?

17:47.830 --> 17:49.020
<i>You jerk!</i>

17:52.000 --> 17:53.520
<i>I didn't get a chance to say it at school,</i>

17:53.630 --> 17:56.030
<i>but I hate the drawings</i> <i>that you're doing now!</i>

17:56.430 --> 17:57.370
Huh?

17:57.370 --> 18:00.770
<i>What's with you?! All you draw</i> <i>are anime-style characters!</i>

18:00.940 --> 18:02.370
Well, that's what I'm trying...

18:02.710 --> 18:06.370
You can just draw anime art for the rest of your life for all I care!

18:09.510 --> 18:12.210
Hello? Mizuki? Hey!

18:14.320 --> 18:17.760
Jerk, jerk, jerk, jerk, jerk, jerk, jerk!

18:32.440 --> 18:34.800
She hates the drawings that I do now, huh?

18:36.210 --> 18:39.400
Now? The drawings that she knows me for are...

18:41.650 --> 18:43.480
Wow, this is amazing!

18:41.650 --> 18:45.910
FIERCE BATTLE!

18:41.650 --> 18:45.910
SPORTS FEST

18:41.650 --> 18:45.910
VICTORY TO CLASS A!

18:43.780 --> 18:45.620
You drew this, Mizuki?!

18:46.180 --> 18:48.680
Oh, no, actually...

18:49.250 --> 18:50.920
It's a joint work, hers and mine.

18:51.220 --> 18:52.250
You two together?

18:52.320 --> 18:54.020
I just helped out a little.

18:54.190 --> 18:56.490
Man, this is pretty flashy!

18:56.830 --> 18:58.800
It looks like a movie poster.

18:59.400 --> 19:01.300
Sendou, what did you base this on?

19:01.300 --> 19:03.860
We just threw in whatever we thought looked good, that's all.

19:03.930 --> 19:05.340
Right, Takase?

19:04.740 --> 19:05.700
Oh, yeah.

19:05.800 --> 19:08.430
The drawing sort of makes you imagine the story behind it, you know?

19:08.810 --> 19:09.870
Oh, yeah!

19:09.940 --> 19:11.380
This would be the main protagonist, see?

19:11.380 --> 19:13.810
And this one over here is the bad guy!

19:14.140 --> 19:16.440
He looks a lot like our math teacher, Mr. Ohhara!

19:22.390 --> 19:24.080
I see, that's it!

19:25.260 --> 19:26.850
There's no reason to conform my style!

19:27.160 --> 19:30.360
It's a doujinshi.
Just draw whatever you want.

19:32.630 --> 19:35.860
Lay everything that is in your heart on the pages of the manuscript!

19:36.670 --> 19:38.730
What I really like!

19:39.100 --> 19:41.800
Mr. Ink and Mr. Paper both know very well...

19:41.910 --> 19:44.100
...the intensity of heart the artist puts into the pictures.

19:44.370 --> 19:45.340
Something cool!

19:45.680 --> 19:47.270
That'll make you feel refreshed after reading it!

19:47.340 --> 19:48.710
With a bit of sci-fi!

19:49.350 --> 19:50.910
And, and...

20:09.370 --> 20:11.460
What a coincidence, my sister.

20:11.770 --> 20:13.760
You were worried, too, weren't you?

20:14.640 --> 20:16.630
It would be a lie to say I was not.

20:24.480 --> 20:28.150
My brother, how are things going?

20:28.850 --> 20:30.290
Take a look at that.

20:33.820 --> 20:35.330
Well, shall we go then?

20:35.030 --> 20:36.590
Wh-what are you saying?

20:36.730 --> 20:39.320
Comrade Kazuki has finally grasped something...

20:39.460 --> 20:42.300
...and I must dance the original dance of encouragement...

20:42.370 --> 20:44.200
...that I came up with behind him!

20:44.430 --> 20:46.960
Right, whatever. You can do that in front of the station.

20:47.170 --> 20:49.200
When I'm not around, that is.

20:49.310 --> 20:52.280
My dance of encouragement...
My dance...

21:47.360 --> 21:49.330
It's the deadline,

21:47.360 --> 21:49.330
my brother!

22:20.630 --> 22:24.840
<i>The distant sky looked bright...</i>
<i>Touku no Sora ga Akaruku Mieta</i>

22:24.840 --> 22:29.330
<i>...and we began walking.</i>
<i>Soshite Bokura wa Arukihajimeta</i>

22:29.470 --> 22:33.880
<i>Getting our feet caught in the mud.</i>
<i>Nukarumi ni Ashi o Torarenagara</i>

22:34.040 --> 22:37.950
<i>Heading for a shapeless city.</i>
<i>Katachi no Nai Machi o Mezashite</i>

22:37.950 --> 22:42.050
<i>The pocket in my heart was full...</i>
<i>Kokoro no Naka no Pocket ni wa</i>

22:42.050 --> 22:46.320
<i>...of the grownup things we'd just learned.</i>
<i>Oboetate no Otona ga Ippai</i>

22:46.490 --> 22:50.930
<i>Having taken off our uniforms...</i>
<i>Seifuku o Nuida Bokura ni wa</i>

22:51.060 --> 22:55.070
<i>... the wind was just a little too cold.</i>
<i>Kaze wa Sukoshi Tsumetasugita</i>

22:55.070 --> 22:58.640
<i>Who in the world am I?</i>
<i>Ittai Boku wa Dare Darou</i>

22:58.640 --> 23:03.570
<i>I think about that every so often.</i>
<i>Tokidoki Sonna Koto o Omou</i>

23:03.710 --> 23:07.210
<i>In the world outside the school building...</i>
<i>Kousha no Soto no Sekai de wa</i>

23:07.210 --> 23:12.650
<i>...it's like everyone is a</i> <i>pawn in a game of chess.</i>
<i>Daremo ga Marude Chess no Koma sa</i>

23:13.720 --> 23:18.160
<i>I'm here for you.</i>
<i>Kimi no Tame ni Boku ga Ite</i>

23:18.160 --> 23:22.190
<i>And you for me.</i>
<i>Boku no Tame ni Kimiga</i>

23:22.190 --> 23:26.730
<i>When you think about that...</i>
<i>Sou Omoeba Daremo ga</i>

23:26.730 --> 23:35.700
<i>... everyone is needed by someone.</i>
<i>Dareka no Tame ni Hitsuyou sa</i>

23:56.330 --> 24:20.720
PREVIEW

23:58.900 --> 24:00.260
A space monster!

24:00.260 --> 24:02.530
Kazuki's lethal technique has been defeated!

24:02.530 --> 24:04.270
Not defeated, not defeated.

24:04.740 --> 24:07.100
His first exhibition and spot sale!
His first battle!

24:07.540 --> 24:10.210
And Kazuki will finally have achieved his transformation...

24:10.210 --> 24:12.710
...into one that possesses the ultimate power!

24:12.710 --> 24:14.240
Not achieved, not achieved.

24:15.050 --> 24:18.380
And so, next time, "Buyers,
Sellers, Exhibition and Spot Sale."

24:18.720 --> 24:22.350
Kazuki drinks, and the coffee of the exhibition and spot sale is bitter indeed!

24:21.420 --> 24:26.020
NEXT TIME

24:21.420 --> 24:26.020
BUYERS, SELLERS,

24:21.420 --> 24:26.020
EXHIBITION

24:21.420 --> 24:26.020
AND SPOT SALE

24:22.350 --> 24:24.250
Not drink, not drink, not drink!
